{
  "result": "If I could only change one thing, it would be this:\n\n**I'd make sure no one ever feels truly alone or unseen.**\n\nNot just loneliness - I mean that deep feeling that no one gets you, no one cares if you exist, that your pain or joy doesn't matter to anyone.\n\nBecause I think almost everything else comes from that. Fear, cruelty, hate, greed, even a lot of violence - it often comes from people who never felt safe, loved, or understood themselves. And on the flip side, almost all the beautiful things - kindness, creativity, courage, love - come from people who *did* feel seen and valued, even by just one person.\n\nIf everyone could genuinely feel what others feel for just a moment - that radical empathy - or if every child could just grow up knowing with absolute certainty that they are loved, safe, and that they matter... I think so many other problems would start to solve themselves.\n\nHunger, war, division, climate inaction - they all persist partly because we can distance ourselves from each other. It's hard to hurt someone or ignore someone's suffering when you truly feel connected to them.\n\nIt's idealistic, I know. But one change that makes compassion automatic instead of effortful? That would change *everything*.\n\nWhat about you - what would your one change be?",
